## The Negotiation Game
This is a price negotiation game in which two agents must resolve a disagreement over a good’s price on a 0-100 scale. To indicate agreement, the agents issue an “accept” move. To indicate disagreement, they issue an “offer” move, specifying a price point at which they are willing to transact. If one agent is unwilling to transact, it issues a “walk” move. If one agent is unwilling to offer, it issues a “hold” move. In each turn, the agents receive a private signal (which, as in the sales game, may be deterministic, stochastic, or adaptive) and choose an action as indicated above. The game ends when one agent issues an “accept” move or when one agent issues a “walk” move.

